SOUNDDVR.DVR device-config method (asm 0x14e): rebase the two method-vector SECTION installs to the
faithful reloc appliers (the crash after patch 347 dispatches the device-select).

FUN_0000_014e is the driver's device-config method reached on the menu via bdcc -> DGROUP:0x508 (section
A, FIST_SB-gated).  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin offset 0x14e:

    14e: cmp al,'N'; je 0x199 (retf)              ; no-device -> nothing
    152: push ds; push ax
    154: mov ax,cs; mov es,ax; mov bx,0x1cd
    15b: lcall [ds:0x43e]                         ; register driver callback cs:0x1cd (engine DGROUP:0x43e)
    15f: pop ax
    160..17c: map device letter -> code (I=1,T=2,A=3,C=3,R=4, else 0)
    17e: mov al,ah; mov ah,0x30
    182: push cs; call 0x833                      ; 0833(0x30|code) = device-select dispatch
    186: pop ds
    187: mov bx,cs; mov si,0x22; lcall [ds:0x12]   ; install method-vector section snd_seg:0x22 (f842 FAR)
    190: mov bx,cs; mov si,0x4e; lcall [ds:0x26]   ; install method-vector section snd_seg:0x4e (f8d2)
    199: retf

Ghidra dropped the FAR service dispatch: the `lcall [ds:0x12]`/`[ds:0x26]` (engine DGROUP service
appliers 0xf842 / 0xf8d2, both in seg 0xf69) were rendered as NEAR host-absolute derefs of module
offsets 0x12/0x26 -> `*(undefined2 *)0x12` = SIGSEGV fault-addr 0x12 (setarch -R + FIST_SB repro).  The
real calls install the driver's own method-vector reloc sections (leading seg word = the relocated driver
load seg + (off,val) pairs) into the engine DGROUP, with bx=cs=driver load seg.  Service 0x12 (f842) is
the plain FAR applier; service 0x26 (f8d2) is a SAVE+install applier that additionally copies the old
DGROUP words back into the section for later restore (via the 019a stop path [ds:0x16]/[ds:0x2a], NOT
reached on the play path).  Both have the identical INSTALL effect DGROUP[off]=val / DGROUP[off+2]=seg,
modelled faithfully via fist_apply_reloc_at(driver_seg, si, is_far=1) -- the same loader-shim applier the
MGAVIDEO driver init uses (patch 035/052) and the sound init 0078 uses for section A (patch 344).  The
f8d2 save-back is documented-omitted (its only consumer, the stop-sound restore, is downstream).

Gated behind fist_sb_enabled(): the whole method is FIST_SB-reachable-only (DGROUP:0x508 stays 0 on the
default boot), and the section installs mutate shared DGROUP state, so the guard is belt-and-suspenders
-> the 26 video flows stay byte-identical.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin offset 0x14e.
--- a/fist_snd.c
+++ b/fist_snd.c
@@ -538,8 +538,22 @@
       }
     }
     FUN_0000_0833(CONCAT11(0x30,uVar1),param_2,extraout_DX,uVar2);
-    (*(code *)fist_icall(fist_snd_base+0x0u+(uint16_t)(*(undefined2 *)0x12)))();
-    (*(code *)fist_icall(fist_snd_base+0x0u+(uint16_t)(*(undefined2 *)0x26)))();
+    /* asm 0x187/0x190: mov bx,cs; mov si,0x22; lcall [ds:0x12]  (f842 FAR applier)
+     *                  mov bx,cs; mov si,0x4e; lcall [ds:0x26]  (f8d2 save+install applier)
+     * both install the driver's method-vector sections snd_seg:0x22 / snd_seg:0x4e into the engine
+     * DGROUP (bx=cs=driver load seg).  Ghidra rendered them as near host-absolute derefs of 0x12/0x26
+     * (SIGSEGV fault-addr 0x12).  The install effect is identical to fist_apply_reloc_at(is_far=1);
+     * f8d2 additionally saves the old DGROUP words back into the section for later restore (via the
+     * 019a stop path [ds:0x16]/[ds:0x2a], not reached on the play path -- documented in docs/audio.md). */
+    {
+      extern int fist_sb_enabled(void);
+      extern int fist_apply_reloc_at(unsigned short,unsigned short,int);
+      if (fist_sb_enabled()) {
+        uint16_t snd_seg = (uint16_t)(fist_snd_base >> 4);
+        fist_apply_reloc_at(snd_seg, 0x22, 1);
+        fist_apply_reloc_at(snd_seg, 0x4e, 1);
+      }
+    }
   }
   return;
 }
